1
00:00:02,799 --> 00:00:05,421
We need to find Kira Tinsley.
She either works for Red John

2
00:00:05,546 --> 00:00:07,340
or she's about to become his next victim.

3
00:00:17,183 --> 00:00:19,185
Who did this to you?
Tell me.

4
00:00:19,685 --> 00:00:20,978
Jane, what did she say?

5
00:00:21,103 --> 00:00:24,273
She told me Red John has
a tattoo on his left shoulder...

6
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:25,650
Three dots.

7
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:27,485
That's my leverage.

8
00:01:41,475 --> 00:01:43,352
- "Jane."
- Hello, Lisbon.

9
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:45,896
"Jane, don't do this,
not without me."

10
00:01:46,355 --> 00:01:47,732
Listen, I'm sorry.

11
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:50,067
"Jane, I am begging you.
You're in danger!"

12
00:01:50,484 --> 00:01:54,322
- It's gonna be okay. I'm gonna be okay.
- "No, you're not."

13
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:56,407
"You do this and you're throwing
your life away."

14
00:01:57,575 --> 00:02:00,703
- Bye, Lisbon.
- "Jane... No."

15
00:03:09,878 --> 00:03:11,672
- "A tattoo?"
- Yes.

16
00:03:11,797 --> 00:03:14,633
- That we can use to identify Red John?
- Yes.

17
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:18,220
That's great. So all we have to do is check
each one of the suspects one by one

18
00:03:18,345 --> 00:03:19,638
until we find out
who has the tattoo.

19
00:03:19,972 --> 00:03:22,516
- No.
- Why not?

20
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:26,645
Red John doesn't know
I know about the tattoo.

21
00:03:27,563 --> 00:03:28,647
Okay.

22
00:03:28,772 --> 00:03:32,026
{\an8}So if we start checking suspects
it's very likely that Red John will find out.

23
00:03:32,151 --> 00:03:34,528
{\an8}And disappear before we have
a chance of getting him.

24
00:03:34,653 --> 00:03:35,696
{\an8}Exactly.

25
00:03:35,904 --> 00:03:37,281
{\an8}Then what do you wanna do?

26
00:03:37,990 --> 00:03:40,868
{\an8}Gather all five suspects together
at the same place, same time

27
00:03:40,993 --> 00:03:44,705
{\an8}- and then start checking for the tattoo.
- And how do we do that?

28
00:03:45,456 --> 00:03:48,167
{\an8}- We'll ask them.
- And you think they'll agree?

29
00:03:49,585 --> 00:03:51,420
{\an8}Wasn't planning on giving them
a choice.

30
00:03:52,796 --> 00:03:54,465
{\an8}Even so, there's a problem.

31
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:57,384
{\an8}Bret Stiles...he's wanted by the F.B.I.
in connection to two homicides.

32
00:03:57,509 --> 00:03:59,637
Yeah. Cold cases
from over 20 years ago.

33
00:03:59,887 --> 00:04:03,057
You're kidding. After all this time
the F.B.I. is moving in now?

34
00:04:03,182 --> 00:04:04,266
{\an8}Well, they must have found
something new...

35
00:04:04,391 --> 00:04:06,894
{\an8}- Forensics, a witness.
- Well, where's Stiles?

36
00:04:07,019 --> 00:04:08,437
{\an8}Well, that's the thing.
Nobody knows.

37
00:04:08,562 --> 00:04:11,231
{\an8}Not even the F.B.I.
Stiles disappeared weeks ago.

38
00:04:11,940 --> 00:04:14,151
{\an8}- We'll find him.
- How?

39
00:04:15,277 --> 00:04:17,821
{\an8}I don't know, but we'll find him.
We have to.

40
00:04:20,324 --> 00:04:22,409
{\an8}- I'm on board with your plan.
- Good.

41
00:04:23,243 --> 00:04:24,411
On one condition.

42
00:04:25,788 --> 00:04:27,873
{\an8}I wanna be there
when you reveal Red John.

43
00:04:30,042 --> 00:04:32,378
{\an8}- Okay.
- Seriously.

44
00:04:33,087 --> 00:04:35,214
- I said okay.
- Yeah, but you didn't mean it.

45
00:04:35,339 --> 00:04:37,132
Did I not?
How can you tell?

46
00:04:37,424 --> 00:04:40,594
- This is non-negotiable, Jane.
- I agree 100%.

47
00:04:46,433 --> 00:04:48,519
{\an8}I think I've made myself clear, agents.

48
00:04:48,936 --> 00:04:51,605
{\an8}I have no knowledge of Bret Stiles'
whereabouts.

49
00:04:51,730 --> 00:04:55,025
{\an8}Yes Mr. Cooper, and we've
made it clear that we're not buying it.

50
00:04:55,150 --> 00:04:56,610
{\an8}Stiles leaves you
in charge of Visualize

51
00:04:56,735 --> 00:04:58,487
{\an8}but he keeps you in the dark
about where he's hiding?

52
00:04:58,612 --> 00:04:59,780
{\an8}Doesn't make sense.

53
00:04:59,905 --> 00:05:04,076
{\an8}Stiles has and always will put
the church's needs before his own.

54
00:05:04,201 --> 00:05:05,536
{\an8}This time is no different.

55
00:05:06,036 --> 00:05:08,122
{\an8}He doesn't want me to know
because he wants to protect me.

56
00:05:08,247 --> 00:05:09,957
And because
he doesn't want to be found.

57
00:05:10,624 --> 00:05:13,252
I doubt Bret Stiles is worried
about being found.

58
00:05:13,794 --> 00:05:15,045
You seem confident.

59
00:05:16,213 --> 00:05:17,464
{\an8}Call it faith.

60
00:05:18,549 --> 00:05:24,054
{\an8}You see, Stiles' time in our...
Reality is limited.

61
00:05:24,888 --> 00:05:27,433
{\an8}As we speak he's preparing
his mind and body

62
00:05:27,558 --> 00:05:31,103
{\an8}for a departure from the confines
of our material world.

63
00:05:31,603 --> 00:05:32,896
He's dying?

64
00:05:35,816 --> 00:05:39,403
That is a very naive
very ignorant way of looking at it.

65
00:05:40,362 --> 00:05:43,574
{\an8}Bret Stiles is not dying.
Bret Stiles cannot die.

66
00:05:43,866 --> 00:05:46,285
He is elevating himself
to another plane

67
00:05:46,410 --> 00:05:50,164
{\an8}one lesser men like ourselves
can only strive to reach.

68
00:05:54,168 --> 00:05:57,171
{\an8}And one some of us obviously
can't comprehend.

69
00:06:14,354 --> 00:06:16,774
- Coffee... one cream, one sugar.
-Thanks, Russell.

70
00:06:17,483 --> 00:06:18,984
Forensics is here
when you're ready.

71
00:06:19,651 --> 00:06:20,944
Send them over.

72
00:06:22,029 --> 00:06:24,907
Get his I.D. for me, will you?
You know how I am about heights.

73
00:06:25,741 --> 00:06:26,784
Sure.

74
00:06:27,367 --> 00:06:29,661
Oh, and, someone's here
to see you.

75
00:06:35,334 --> 00:06:36,460
Thanks.

76
00:06:41,298 --> 00:06:44,009
There's been a breakthrough
in the Red John investigation.

77
00:06:44,468 --> 00:06:48,388
I have some new information.
Some very significant information.

78
00:06:49,515 --> 00:06:52,684
- Okay. What is it?
- No, no. Not yet.

79
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:57,314
I'm not sure who I can trust.
I'm not even sure I can trust you.

80
00:06:58,148 --> 00:07:00,567
Red John has some
very powerful allies.

81
00:07:01,777 --> 00:07:03,695
Patrick, come on.

82
00:07:07,699 --> 00:07:10,118
Okay, but not here.

83
00:07:10,619 --> 00:07:12,788
Meet me at 8:00
on Thursday night.

84
00:07:13,455 --> 00:07:14,748
Thursday? Why?

85
00:07:14,873 --> 00:07:17,209
I need time to find
a safe place to meet.

86
00:07:18,961 --> 00:07:20,963
Fine. Where?

87
00:07:21,088 --> 00:07:24,174
- I'll let you know the day of.
- This is crazy.

88
00:07:24,299 --> 00:07:27,469
I've made the mistake of underestimating
Red John a number of times now.

89
00:07:27,594 --> 00:07:29,388
I don't wanna make
that mistake again.

90
00:07:29,513 --> 00:07:32,516
If you want the information,
it's on my terms.

91
00:07:34,393 --> 00:07:35,435
Okay.

92
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,813
Thursday night.

93
00:08:15,434 --> 00:08:17,060
This is Sheriff McAllister.

94
00:08:18,437 --> 00:08:20,647
Sheriff? Patrick Jane.

95
00:08:22,065 --> 00:08:23,901
Hello, Patrick.
How are things?

96
00:08:24,568 --> 00:08:26,612
Good. Good.

97
00:08:27,154 --> 00:08:29,448
I'm calling because
I had a question.

98
00:08:29,573 --> 00:08:30,824
Shoot.

99
00:08:31,325 --> 00:08:34,745
Last month when I was in Napa
you said that you were at my disposal.

100
00:08:35,329 --> 00:08:38,749
- Yes, I remember.
- Did you mean what you said?

101
00:08:39,333 --> 00:08:43,003
- I like to think I'm a man of my word.
- Oh, I don't doubt it.

102
00:08:43,795 --> 00:08:45,672
But can I count on you
for your help?

103
00:08:46,298 --> 00:08:49,217
- "Can I count on you?"
- Of course.

104
00:08:49,927 --> 00:08:53,221
Thursday night at 8:00
I'll need your help.

105
00:08:53,889 --> 00:08:55,307
Well, then you've got it.

106
00:08:56,224 --> 00:08:57,267
Thank you.

107
00:08:57,643 --> 00:08:59,728
I'll let you know where to be
the day of.

108
00:09:00,938 --> 00:09:03,190
- Patrick?
- Yeah?

109
00:09:04,107 --> 00:09:05,984
This is about Red John,
isn't it?

110
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,780
Thursday night.

111
00:09:24,002 --> 00:09:27,422
- They're ready for you, sir.
- Thank you, Evelyn.

112
00:09:28,632 --> 00:09:30,342
Also, this came for you.

113
00:11:28,794 --> 00:11:32,464
You are here tonight
to witness my ascension.

114
00:11:33,757 --> 00:11:39,096
My ascension from this world
to a world beyond.

115
00:11:40,597 --> 00:11:42,974
Do not mourn me, my children

116
00:11:44,643 --> 00:11:49,731
for this is not a passing
but a departure.

117
00:11:52,192 --> 00:11:53,485
And I promise...

118
00:11:55,362 --> 00:12:00,867
I... Will... Return!

119
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:19,300
Listen to me, Don, you don't have
a mistress.

120
00:12:19,425 --> 00:12:21,761
You have a vindictive screwball
who's about to ruin your life.

121
00:12:22,595 --> 00:12:24,931
Yes, well, it's very lucky for you
my job is to fix problems

122
00:12:25,056 --> 00:12:26,141
so here's what you're gonna do.

123
00:12:26,266 --> 00:12:28,101
You are gonna write her
a check...

124
00:12:28,226 --> 00:12:29,936
It is gonna be
a very big check...

125
00:12:30,061 --> 00:12:32,313
And then you are gonna pray
that this problem goes away.

126
00:12:34,149 --> 00:12:35,817
If it doesn't,
don't worry, Don.

127
00:12:35,942 --> 00:12:38,153
There are plenty of ways
to keep a woman quiet. Okay?

128
00:12:38,278 --> 00:12:40,321
All right.
I gotta go. All right.

129
00:12:48,246 --> 00:12:49,289
Hello.

130
00:12:50,290 --> 00:12:52,917
- You're late.
- It's good to see you, too, Teresa.

131
00:12:53,251 --> 00:12:55,712
Uh, excuse me, can I get
coffee, black, please?

132
00:12:55,837 --> 00:12:57,130
- Sure.
- Thanks.

133
00:12:57,922 --> 00:12:59,465
So why am I here
at 8:00 a.m.?

134
00:13:00,341 --> 00:13:02,510
I need help with an investigation.

135
00:13:03,428 --> 00:13:04,554
What investigation?

136
00:13:04,846 --> 00:13:07,807
- It's not important.
- Really? It is if you want my help.

137
00:13:09,851 --> 00:13:11,060
I can't tell you.

138
00:13:11,186 --> 00:13:13,062
Come on, Teresa.
I know you better than that.

139
00:13:13,188 --> 00:13:15,440
What, you and Jane got something
going on with the Red John case?

140
00:13:17,442 --> 00:13:20,028
- Maybe.
- "Maybe." yeah, right.

141
00:13:21,487 --> 00:13:23,323
What is with all the secrecy?

142
00:13:24,365 --> 00:13:26,201
Seriously, why are you
always holding out on me?

143
00:13:26,326 --> 00:13:28,077
You don't think I'm Red John,
do you?

144
00:13:31,039 --> 00:13:32,373
You do, don't you?

145
00:13:34,959 --> 00:13:36,169
Tell you what.

146
00:13:36,294 --> 00:13:37,754
You want to question me,
you arrest me.

147
00:13:37,879 --> 00:13:39,380
Otherwise, you leave me
the hell out of this.

148
00:13:39,505 --> 00:13:42,050
Sit down. Sit.

149
00:13:47,305 --> 00:13:49,724
If asking's not gonna work,
I won't ask.

150
00:13:50,183 --> 00:13:51,643
You're no longer
with the CBI.

151
00:13:51,768 --> 00:13:54,479
You don't get the same protection
law enforcement gets.

152
00:13:54,604 --> 00:13:56,439
- What, you threatening me?
- No, Jane is.

153
00:13:57,106 --> 00:13:58,691
He wants to see you
tomorrow night.

154
00:14:02,570 --> 00:14:05,114
If you don't show up, he will
assume you're Red John.

155
00:14:05,406 --> 00:14:08,076
And, Ray, he will come after you.

156
00:14:09,118 --> 00:14:10,536
You gotta be kidding me.

157
00:14:11,704 --> 00:14:14,123
You know Jane.
You know what happened to him.

158
00:14:14,249 --> 00:14:16,251
You know what Red John
did to him.

159
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:19,462
If I were you,
I wouldn't test him.

160
00:14:20,171 --> 00:14:21,714
I'm not afraid
of Patrick Jane.

161
00:14:21,839 --> 00:14:23,466
Well, what's the problem
with showing up?

162
00:14:26,844 --> 00:14:31,182
If I do this, will you and Jane drop
the whole that "I'm Red John" business?

163
00:14:31,307 --> 00:14:33,101
For once and for all.

164
00:14:35,478 --> 00:14:37,897
- What time?
- 8:00.

165
00:14:39,774 --> 00:14:40,858
I'm not done.

166
00:14:43,236 --> 00:14:45,321
There's one more thing
that I need.

167
00:14:45,780 --> 00:14:47,073
You're killing me here.

168
00:14:49,075 --> 00:14:50,910
- Stiles.
- Yeah?

169
00:14:51,035 --> 00:14:52,745
- Where is he?
- I can't help you.

170
00:14:52,870 --> 00:14:56,416
Come on, Ray, you've been
with Visualize for years.

171
00:14:58,251 --> 00:15:00,211
I don't want to arrest him.
I just want to talk to him.

172
00:15:02,463 --> 00:15:04,382
You do this,
and I will owe you.

173
00:15:04,882 --> 00:15:08,177
And in your line of work, sooner or later
you're gonna need a favor.

174
00:15:11,431 --> 00:15:13,266
So Ray Haffner told me that Stiles

175
00:15:13,391 --> 00:15:16,352
uses a private jet to move
around the country undetected.

176
00:15:16,477 --> 00:15:18,730
Belongs to a guy
named Ryan Parks.

177
00:15:19,522 --> 00:15:21,065
Parks. Got it.
I'll check it out.

178
00:15:21,566 --> 00:15:24,193
- Has Jane been in yet?
- No, I haven't heard from him.

179
00:15:49,427 --> 00:15:50,470
Mr. Lamotte?

180
00:15:51,304 --> 00:15:53,181
Yeah? Can I help you?

181
00:15:53,473 --> 00:15:55,224
Agents Cho and Rigsby
from the CBI.

182
00:15:55,350 --> 00:15:57,018
We were wondering if you could
answer a few questions for us.

183
00:15:57,143 --> 00:15:58,186
Sure.

184
00:15:58,311 --> 00:16:02,023
A G6 landed here late last night
tail number N550MT.

185
00:16:02,148 --> 00:16:03,399
It would have been
around 11:00.

186
00:16:03,524 --> 00:16:05,026
I remember.
What about it?

187
00:16:05,151 --> 00:16:06,361
Do you know who was
on the flight?

188
00:16:06,486 --> 00:16:10,031
No. Private aircraft aren't required
to provide passenger manifests.

189
00:16:10,156 --> 00:16:12,158
Did you happen to see anyone
who was getting off the plane?

190
00:16:12,283 --> 00:16:13,826
No. Sorry.

191
00:16:14,077 --> 00:16:16,454
Oh, but whoever it was had
a car service pick him up.

192
00:16:16,579 --> 00:16:17,705
They might be able
to help you.

193
00:16:17,830 --> 00:16:20,416
You don't happen to have the name
of that car service by any chance?

194
00:16:20,541 --> 00:16:21,584
Yes, I do.

195
00:16:23,336 --> 00:16:24,879
So what happened
with the car service?

196
00:16:25,004 --> 00:16:26,839
Well, they said that they picked up
a silver-haired man

197
00:16:26,964 --> 00:16:29,050
with a British accent
from the airport last night.

198
00:16:29,175 --> 00:16:30,593
- Stiles.
- We think so.

199
00:16:30,718 --> 00:16:31,886
- Well, where'd he go?
- The address

200
00:16:32,011 --> 00:16:34,555
was for the Ecuadorian
consulate in San Francisco.

201
00:16:34,680 --> 00:16:36,599
Good job.
You two go and check it out.

202
00:16:37,850 --> 00:16:40,103
You know what?
Van Pelt, why don't you go alone?

203
00:16:40,228 --> 00:16:42,605
Stiles likes you. Maybe we can
use that to our advantage.

204
00:16:45,316 --> 00:16:46,859
Is... There a problem?

205
00:16:47,026 --> 00:16:48,319
- No.
- No.

206
00:16:51,739 --> 00:16:53,116
- I'll be fine.
- I know.

207
00:16:53,574 --> 00:16:54,909
- It's my job.
- I know.

208
00:16:55,284 --> 00:16:56,327
Hey.

209
00:16:56,828 --> 00:16:59,705
- I love you.
- I know.

210
00:17:15,054 --> 00:17:16,639
- Hey, Lisbon.
- Where are you?

211
00:17:16,889 --> 00:17:19,434
- Oh, just running some errands.
- "Everything okay?"

212
00:17:19,559 --> 00:17:21,310
Yeah, right as rain.
What's up?

213
00:17:21,561 --> 00:17:22,812
"Haffner's in."

214
00:17:23,271 --> 00:17:24,814
Good. What about Stiles?

215
00:17:24,939 --> 00:17:28,067
Van Pelt may have a bead on his location.
She's checking it out now.

216
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:31,279
That leaves one more Red John
suspect left to talk to.

217
00:17:31,404 --> 00:17:33,781
Yes. Bertram.
I'm on my way to his office.

218
00:17:33,906 --> 00:17:35,324
- You want to meet me there?
- "All right."

219
00:17:41,122 --> 00:17:45,751
Grace Van Pelt.
Well... How lovely to see you again.

220
00:17:48,379 --> 00:17:50,631
Well... So, please sit.

221
00:17:50,756 --> 00:17:54,010
- To what do I owe this pleasure?
- Jane.

222
00:17:55,052 --> 00:17:56,220
He needs a favor.

223
00:17:57,805 --> 00:17:59,474
Clever, him, sending you.

224
00:18:00,516 --> 00:18:03,644
So exactly what can I do
for Patrick Jane?

225
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:07,732
He would like to meet with you.
Tomorrow night at 8:00.

226
00:18:10,443 --> 00:18:12,445
You've changed since
we last met.

227
00:18:12,570 --> 00:18:14,989
- You're married.
- Yes.

228
00:18:15,990 --> 00:18:18,117
Oh, don't tell me you married
that genial oaf.

229
00:18:19,827 --> 00:18:22,788
Oh. Oh, well.
Congratulations.

230
00:18:22,914 --> 00:18:24,207
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

231
00:18:25,458 --> 00:18:28,044
So... Will you meet
with Jane?

232
00:18:28,169 --> 00:18:32,548
Ah... You know, nothing would please
me more than to meet with him.

233
00:18:32,673 --> 00:18:34,800
I mean, really,
I would love to. But...

234
00:18:36,010 --> 00:18:38,471
Unfortunately,
my circumstances...

235
00:18:38,596 --> 00:18:40,264
It's probably
not gonna happen.

236
00:18:41,307 --> 00:18:42,892
You mean
because of the F.B.I.?

237
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:46,145
You have been doing
your homework.

238
00:18:47,021 --> 00:18:48,397
They don't know I'm here.

239
00:18:49,065 --> 00:18:50,816
Which means they don't know
you're here.

240
00:18:51,359 --> 00:18:53,528
But they will if you don't agree
to meet with Jane.

241
00:18:54,445 --> 00:18:56,781
You have changed,
haven't you?

242
00:19:00,535 --> 00:19:04,038
Have you ever been
to Ecuador, by any chance?

243
00:19:04,163 --> 00:19:05,289
No.

244
00:19:06,249 --> 00:19:09,252
I was there...oh, God,
years and years ago

245
00:19:09,794 --> 00:19:11,796
Doing missionary work.

246
00:19:12,463 --> 00:19:15,550
Lovely people.
Oh, yeah, but-but...

247
00:19:15,675 --> 00:19:17,593
There was a young man there...

248
00:19:18,135 --> 00:19:22,473
he was underprivileged,
ferociously ambitious.

249
00:19:23,015 --> 00:19:24,642
I saw something in him.

250
00:19:25,142 --> 00:19:27,937
So I decided
to try and help him.

251
00:19:28,062 --> 00:19:30,898
You know, I paid for his school fees
that sort of thing.

252
00:19:31,023 --> 00:19:33,568
Nothing really much,
but wouldn't you know it?

253
00:19:33,693 --> 00:19:38,573
All these years later, that same man
is now minister of state.

254
00:19:39,115 --> 00:19:40,533
I'm happy for him.

255
00:19:40,908 --> 00:19:45,621
Anyway, he invited me to stay in this
palatial consulate.

256
00:19:45,913 --> 00:19:49,333
This morsel of foreign soil.

257
00:19:49,458 --> 00:19:52,044
Foreign soil, which,
as you know

258
00:19:52,545 --> 00:19:58,509
is outside the jurisdiction of you,
the F.B.I. and all U.S. law enforcement.

259
00:19:58,676 --> 00:20:02,555
So, you see, Gracie your idle threats
are just that.

260
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:04,807
Well, it's been so lovely
seeing you again.

261
00:20:04,932 --> 00:20:07,268
Please give my best
to Mr. Jane.

262
00:20:07,852 --> 00:20:09,979
Close the door
on your way out!

263
00:20:16,652 --> 00:20:19,155
- It's gonna be fine.
- Thanks. I feel a lot better.

264
00:20:21,073 --> 00:20:22,116
Come on in.

265
00:20:25,953 --> 00:20:27,413
We've made
a breakthrough, sir.

266
00:20:28,539 --> 00:20:30,416
- In...
- The Red John case.

267
00:20:31,375 --> 00:20:33,085
We're close to identifying him.

268
00:20:34,170 --> 00:20:36,255
Well, then this
is fantastic news.

269
00:20:36,714 --> 00:20:39,508
After all these years. You...
You really think you've got him?

270
00:20:39,634 --> 00:20:40,968
I do.

271
00:20:43,054 --> 00:20:45,556
I'll know the second you
have something concrete.

272
00:20:45,681 --> 00:20:47,892
- You will, sir.
- And I want to be there when you end this.

273
00:20:48,517 --> 00:20:50,061
I was hoping you'd say that.

274
00:21:24,428 --> 00:21:25,721
Yeah, it's me.

275
00:21:27,056 --> 00:21:30,434
I just had a very interesting
conversation with Patrick Jane.

276
00:21:32,853 --> 00:21:33,896
How'd it go with Bertram?

277
00:21:34,021 --> 00:21:36,524
- He's in. What about Stiles?
- Not so good.

278
00:21:36,649 --> 00:21:38,734
- Did you find him?
- Yes.

279
00:21:38,859 --> 00:21:40,194
Then what's the problem?

280
00:21:41,654 --> 00:21:43,572
He's at the Ecuadorian consulate.

281
00:21:43,698 --> 00:21:45,741
As long as he's there,
we can't touch him.

282
00:21:47,326 --> 00:21:48,661
What do you want to do?

283
00:21:49,870 --> 00:21:51,205
I'll handle Stiles.

284
00:21:51,330 --> 00:21:53,457
He's not gonna come with you.
He doesn't have to.

285
00:21:53,582 --> 00:21:54,917
I'll be persuasive.

286
00:21:57,503 --> 00:21:58,587
What is that?

287
00:22:08,305 --> 00:22:11,559
A shotgun. You sure it's big enough?

288
00:22:17,356 --> 00:22:19,358
We need to talk
about tomorrow night.

289
00:22:19,483 --> 00:22:21,902
- I've already told you.
- Just hear me out, please.

290
00:22:23,988 --> 00:22:27,241
- You don't want me to be there.
- No, I don't.

291
00:22:27,783 --> 00:22:29,660
You don't want to be there
because you think

292
00:22:29,785 --> 00:22:32,413
I'm gonna try and stop you
from killing Red John.

293
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:34,415
Are you saying that you won't?

294
00:22:34,999 --> 00:22:38,836
What I'm saying is some men...
Men like Red John...

295
00:22:39,253 --> 00:22:41,922
They don't deserve a trial.
They don't deserve a jury.

296
00:22:43,257 --> 00:22:45,217
They deserve what they have
coming to them.

297
00:22:46,385 --> 00:22:47,762
Wait, let me get this straight.

298
00:22:47,887 --> 00:22:50,806
After close to 20 years
working in law enforcement

299
00:22:50,931 --> 00:22:52,767
you're just...
you're changing your mind?

300
00:22:53,267 --> 00:22:54,643
About Red John? Yes.

301
00:22:56,687 --> 00:22:57,980
I'm surprised, Lisbon.

302
00:22:59,690 --> 00:23:03,068
- What, you don't believe me?
- Heavens, no.

303
00:23:03,819 --> 00:23:05,196
You're the most honest
person I know.

304
00:23:05,321 --> 00:23:07,448
You would never lie,
not about something like this.

305
00:23:08,824 --> 00:23:11,827
- Right?
- Right.

306
00:23:12,661 --> 00:23:15,706
- Tomorrow night then.
- Tomorrow night.

307
00:23:41,246 --> 00:23:43,123
Patrick, dear boy.

308
00:23:43,415 --> 00:23:44,458
Well, how are you?

309
00:23:45,334 --> 00:23:46,877
Well, I'm not your boy.

310
00:23:47,419 --> 00:23:51,548
Oh, I see. So this is
not a social meeting, eh?

311
00:23:52,174 --> 00:23:54,259
You're gonna meet me
tonight at 8:00.

312
00:23:56,136 --> 00:23:57,930
- Patrick...
- No, you listen to me.

313
00:23:59,014 --> 00:24:00,641
You're gonna meet me
tonight at 8:00

314
00:24:00,766 --> 00:24:02,726
or I'm gonna come back here,
and when I do

315
00:24:02,851 --> 00:24:05,646
you will need more than these
walls to keep you safe.

316
00:24:06,396 --> 00:24:09,858
Threats?
That's so out of character.

317
00:24:09,983 --> 00:24:12,736
- I mean every word of it.
- Yes.

318
00:24:14,446 --> 00:24:15,822
I believe you do.

319
00:24:17,741 --> 00:24:19,368
But you see, Patrick

320
00:24:20,452 --> 00:24:23,455
a dying man does not fear death.

321
00:24:23,580 --> 00:24:24,706
Oh, please.

322
00:24:24,831 --> 00:24:27,751
This charade might work on your disciples.
It doesn't work on me.

323
00:24:29,461 --> 00:24:31,630
You think too highly of me.

324
00:24:32,839 --> 00:24:36,426
Unfortunately
it's not a charade.

325
00:24:40,305 --> 00:24:41,598
How long have you got?

326
00:24:44,017 --> 00:24:45,394
It's spread to the blood.

327
00:24:45,519 --> 00:24:47,646
There's nothing they can do.
I don't know...

328
00:24:47,771 --> 00:24:49,564
two weeks, a month.

329
00:24:51,483 --> 00:24:52,651
You see...

330
00:24:54,987 --> 00:24:56,405
it's not personal.

331
00:24:56,947 --> 00:24:58,240
It's just that...

332
00:24:58,991 --> 00:25:01,576
my time now
is very precious.

333
00:25:02,577 --> 00:25:04,079
I'm still gonna need you tonight.

334
00:25:06,081 --> 00:25:09,751
For God sake, why?
What's so damned important?

335
00:25:10,502 --> 00:25:11,712
Red John.

336
00:25:12,254 --> 00:25:13,463
I'm close.

337
00:25:14,047 --> 00:25:15,590
Closer than I've ever been.

338
00:25:21,138 --> 00:25:22,764
Red John...

339
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:30,647
Look... nothing would give me more
pleasure than to be with you there tonight.

340
00:25:30,772 --> 00:25:31,815
But?

341
00:25:32,691 --> 00:25:36,945
There's more to this than you know.
There's... there's more keeping me here.

342
00:25:37,070 --> 00:25:40,032
- The F.B.I.?
- Yeah, as a matter of fact.

343
00:25:40,323 --> 00:25:41,950
You know,
they tracked me here.

344
00:25:42,075 --> 00:25:44,536
They're just waiting for me to leave
so they can arrest me.

345
00:25:44,703 --> 00:25:48,165
Look, I'm not choosing to stay here
but I'm trapped.

346
00:25:48,957 --> 00:25:51,585
So the F.B.I.'s the only thing
that's keeping you here?

347
00:25:55,380 --> 00:25:57,716
"Eyes up. We've got movement
at the front entrance."

348
00:25:59,384 --> 00:26:02,054
"That's a Visualize car.
I think they're sneaking someone out."

349
00:26:02,929 --> 00:26:04,222
"Get ready to move."

350
00:26:05,015 --> 00:26:06,725
"Go now! Go! Go! Go!"

351
00:26:25,827 --> 00:26:27,996
Don't move! Your hands
on your steering wheel.

352
00:26:29,081 --> 00:26:30,540
Keep your hands
where we can see 'em.

353
00:26:31,958 --> 00:26:33,085
Hello, gentlemen.

354
00:26:33,627 --> 00:26:35,253
Something I can help you with?

355
00:27:08,120 --> 00:27:09,496
Stiles is in.

356
00:27:10,831 --> 00:27:13,583
We'd better get going.
We've got a long drive ahead of us.

357
00:27:15,919 --> 00:27:19,756
Come on. Take him.

358
00:27:54,249 --> 00:27:56,459
Well, then SAC P.D.'s just gonna
have to wait.

359
00:27:56,918 --> 00:27:59,754
Look, I don't wanna pull rank...
but I will.

360
00:28:03,258 --> 00:28:04,885
Kevin, I gotta call you back.

361
00:28:14,644 --> 00:28:16,479
I'll be needing a car.

362
00:28:50,972 --> 00:28:54,893
- What are we doing?
- I wanna see the sunset.

363
00:29:28,485 --> 00:29:30,653
There's something I want
to tell you, Lisbon.

364
00:29:33,448 --> 00:29:35,533
Something I should have said
a long time ago.

365
00:29:37,577 --> 00:29:39,913
I want to thank you
for everything that you've done.

366
00:29:40,038 --> 00:29:41,956
- You can thank me later.
- No, I...

367
00:29:43,708 --> 00:29:45,335
I need to say this now.

368
00:29:50,673 --> 00:29:54,094
You have... no idea
what you've meant to me.

369
00:29:56,888 --> 00:29:58,390
What you mean to me.

370
00:30:02,185 --> 00:30:03,436
Thank you.

371
00:30:20,495 --> 00:30:22,789
I almost forgot.
I have a surprise for you.

372
00:30:24,124 --> 00:30:25,625
Wait here.

373
00:30:38,763 --> 00:30:39,806
Jane?

374
00:30:40,473 --> 00:30:41,599
Jane!

375
00:32:10,605 --> 00:32:12,482
Hello! Hey!

376
00:34:38,086 --> 00:34:39,379
Hey! Stop!

377
00:34:40,505 --> 00:34:41,547
Police.

378
00:34:44,676 --> 00:34:48,179
My name is Teresa Lisbon. I am an agent
with the California Bureau of Investigation

379
00:34:48,304 --> 00:34:50,598
and I need to borrow your car.
It's an emergency.

380
00:34:50,723 --> 00:34:52,975
- What?! No way.
- Get out. Now. Come on.

381
00:34:53,601 --> 00:34:57,271
- Come on.
- This is outrageous. I'm calling the police.

382
00:34:57,397 --> 00:34:58,856
Good idea. Thanks.

383
00:35:02,235 --> 00:35:04,112
Wh... damn!

384
00:35:13,913 --> 00:35:15,790
- "Jane."
- Hello, Lisbon.

385
00:35:15,915 --> 00:35:19,836
- Jane, don't do this, not without me.
- Listen, I'm sorry.

386
00:35:19,961 --> 00:35:22,130
Jane, I am begging you.
You're in danger!

387
00:35:22,588 --> 00:35:25,174
It's gonna be okay.
I'm gonna be okay.

388
00:35:25,550 --> 00:35:28,678
No, you're not. You do this
and you're throwing your life away.

389
00:35:29,679 --> 00:35:31,222
- Bye, Lisbon.
- "Jane..."

390
00:35:31,931 --> 00:35:32,974
No.

391
00:36:57,016 --> 00:36:58,810
Oh. Hello, Patrick.

392
00:37:00,019 --> 00:37:01,312
Am I early?

393
00:37:02,438 --> 00:37:04,565
No, no. Right on time.
Have a seat.

394
00:37:17,977 --> 00:37:19,770
"9-1-1.
What's your emergency?"

395
00:37:19,895 --> 00:37:23,023
This is agent Teresa Lisbon
with the California Bureau of Investigation.

396
00:37:23,149 --> 00:37:26,777
I need officers
at 1309 cedar street in Malibu.

397
00:37:27,027 --> 00:37:29,530
I have an agent who needs
immediate assistance.

398
00:37:32,867 --> 00:37:34,660
I brought you five together
for a reason.

399
00:37:34,785 --> 00:37:36,787
Some of you may know
that reason.

400
00:37:38,205 --> 00:37:39,707
Some of you may have guessed.

401
00:37:41,167 --> 00:37:42,585
But one of you here...

402
00:37:45,504 --> 00:37:46,797
Is Red John.

403
00:37:49,175 --> 00:37:51,093
What?! One of us?

404
00:37:51,802 --> 00:37:54,221
One of us here is Red John?

405
00:37:54,889 --> 00:37:56,724
Well, that's very interesting.

406
00:37:57,391 --> 00:37:59,143
- Who is it?
- I don't know.

407
00:38:00,269 --> 00:38:01,604
And that's what we're
gonna find out.

408
00:38:01,729 --> 00:38:04,940
Wait, you're trying to say that one
of us in this room is a serial killer?

409
00:38:05,065 --> 00:38:06,275
- I know it.
- No, this is crazy.

410
00:38:06,400 --> 00:38:07,860
I can assure you, it's not.

411
00:38:08,444 --> 00:38:10,780
Well, I can assure you
I'm not sticking around for this crap.

412
00:38:16,786 --> 00:38:17,828
Sit down.

413
00:38:18,537 --> 00:38:20,581
Do not move
toward the door.

414
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:22,374
No one is leaving.

415
00:38:23,918 --> 00:38:25,336
Take it easy, Patrick.

416
00:38:26,587 --> 00:38:27,963
Do I look distressed?

417
00:38:31,675 --> 00:38:32,718
Don't.

418
00:38:33,844 --> 00:38:35,054
I will shoot you.

419
00:38:36,680 --> 00:38:38,599
That goes for the rest
of you as well.

420
00:38:40,184 --> 00:38:43,813
Take out your weapons slowly,
place them on the floor

421
00:38:44,313 --> 00:38:46,065
and push them toward me.

422
00:38:55,491 --> 00:38:56,700
Thank you.

423
00:38:57,952 --> 00:38:58,994
Thank you.

424
00:39:02,498 --> 00:39:03,541
Okay, Patrick.

425
00:39:03,666 --> 00:39:06,502
This is...
This is enough.

426
00:39:07,086 --> 00:39:08,295
It's gone far enough.

427
00:39:08,754 --> 00:39:10,339
No, we're just getting started.

428
00:39:10,798 --> 00:39:12,925
I've waited ten years
for this moment.

429
00:39:14,134 --> 00:39:16,428
All those years,
Red John has been smart.

430
00:39:16,929 --> 00:39:19,807
One of you has been smart.

431
00:39:20,057 --> 00:39:21,976
Careful.
But not this time.

432
00:39:22,101 --> 00:39:23,644
This time,
you made a mistake.

433
00:39:25,020 --> 00:39:28,190
Kira Tinsley told me something
before she passed.

434
00:39:29,984 --> 00:39:32,444
She told me that her killer...
Red John...

435
00:39:33,445 --> 00:39:34,822
Has a tattoo.

436
00:39:36,282 --> 00:39:40,035
Three dots on his left arm.
On his shoulder.

437
00:39:41,078 --> 00:39:42,413
And you all...

438
00:39:43,664 --> 00:39:45,124
Are gonna show me...

439
00:39:47,751 --> 00:39:48,878
Now.

440
00:39:53,382 --> 00:39:54,842
Let's go. Come on.

441
00:39:56,302 --> 00:39:58,220
That's it. Take it off.

442
00:40:01,515 --> 00:40:02,766
Nonsense.

443
00:40:11,150 --> 00:40:12,318
Very good.

444
00:40:31,211 --> 00:40:32,796
It's not what you think.

445
00:40:33,672 --> 00:40:35,132
- You got it wrong.
- Enough.

446
00:40:35,674 --> 00:40:36,926
I'm not Red John.

447
00:40:38,135 --> 00:40:40,137
Patrick, wait. Patrick!

448
00:40:40,262 --> 00:40:42,389
Look... Here. Look.

449
00:41:00,866 --> 00:41:01,951
On your feet.

450
00:41:02,576 --> 00:41:03,744
Over with those two.

451
00:41:09,333 --> 00:41:10,501
You stay there.

452
00:41:11,585 --> 00:41:12,920
Okay, you three...

453
00:41:13,796 --> 00:41:15,589
Over against that wall...
now.

454
00:41:23,514 --> 00:41:25,057
"Wait! No!"

455
00:41:59,925 --> 00:42:01,093
Jane!

